  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, federal contract obligations in Missouri total $8.6B. These totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial. Obligations are down 38.4% year over year, and federal buying in the state currently runs across a wide spread of agencies with the Department of Defense accounting for the largest share at $5.7B. Other major buyers include the Department of Energy at $2B and civilian agencies such as the Department of Veterans Affairs at $200M and the Department of Agriculture at $193M. Award activity remains substantial: there are 90,380 awards to date with an average award size of $95.3K. The vendor and industry mix shows concentration in aircraft and facilities support, with THE BOEING COMPANY and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC the top suppliers by dollar value. Year-to-date industry leaders include Aircraft Manufacturing at $2.5B and Facilities Support Services at $2.1B. This picture reflects a defense- and energy-weighted procurement profile along with continued demand for specialized manufacturing and support services.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the current level of spending in Missouri?",
        "body": "The spending level reflects large Department of Defense obligations, which total $5.7B. The Department of Energy contributes $2B, so those two agencies together represent the bulk of the $8.6B total. Year-over-year obligations are down 38.4%, which shows fiscal-year-to-date activity is lower than in the prior period. The total number of awards is 90,380 with an average award size of $95.3K, indicating many small and mid-sized transactions alongside large prime awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate federal contracting in Missouri?",
        "body": "Aircraft Manufacturing and Facilities Support Services lead industry obligations at $2.5B and $2.1B respectively. THE BOEING COMPANY and HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC are the top vendors at $3.5B and $2B. Other notable vendors include EVERNORTH FEDERAL SERVICES INC at $697M and WORLD WIDE TECHNOLOGY LLC at $160M. Ammunition and other aircraft-related manufacturing categories also rank among the top industries by dollars."
      }
    ]
  },
